  You are root on a live Arch environment. Nothing here touches any disk
  unless you tell it to — the verifier is READ-ONLY.

  1) WiFi (interactive):   nmtui
        or one-shot:       nmcli device wifi connect "SSID" password "PASSWORD"

  2) Find the wiped disk BY MODEL/SIZE (device letters vary):
        lsblk -o NAME,SIZE,MODEL,SERIAL

  3) Verify it (repo is baked in at /root/Duressd):
        duressd-verify /dev/sdX
        # equivalent to:
        # bash /root/Duressd/tests/physical/verify-wipe.sh /dev/sdX --scenario sdboot-luks

     Add  --baseline /path/to/baseline-dir  for the NVRAM/TPM comparison rows.

  Proof the ESP/boot scrub worked:
     no-boot-fs   -> ESP vfat signature GONE
     marker-absent-> /boot marker GONE from raw sectors (byte-scrubbed)

  4) Reboot check: power-cycle with ONLY the wiped disk attached -> must NOT boot.

